=========================================================================================================
13_scaffold_split.py — Performance under scaffold-grouped outer folds
=========================================================================================================

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Random folds put close analogs of the same chemical series in both the training and the test
  part, which can make a         model look better than it would be on a new series. The scaffold
  runs (SC01, SC09, SC17, SC19) repeated the benchmark         with folds that keep every Bemis-
  Murcko scaffold in a single fold, for the four classical representations and for the
  neural models. This step puts every scaffold result next to its random-fold result, compares the
  classical         representations with each other on the scaffold folds, and tests each neural
  model against them. The scaffold results         are expected to be lower; the question is
  whether the comparisons change.
