~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What these figures show
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Three views of the virtual-screening candidates from step 05 (top ML predictions plus reference
  drugs):         (1) predicted pIC50 per compound - longer bar = more potent; reference drugs
  show where a real, known inhibitor         lands. (2) predicted pIC50 against ligand efficiency
  (LE, potency per heavy atom): the top-right corner is both         potent and efficient, the
  best place for a lead. (3) a multi-metric profile (LE, BEI, LLE, SEI) per compound, to see
  whether high potency is accompanied by good efficiency or comes only from molecular
  size/lipophilicity.         All values are model predictions, not measurements.
